    "ExplanationCorrect": "Under IFRS (IAS 2), LIFO (last-in, first-out) is not permitted as an inventory costing method. U.S. GAAP (ASC 330-10-30-9) allows LIFO, creating a key GAAP vs. IFRS difference frequently tested on the CMA exam. Average cost, FIFO, and specific identification are permitted under both frameworks. This distinction is important for international financial reporting and reconciling U.S.-to-IFRS financial statements.",
