    "Stem": "An operating loss carryforward creates a:",
    "ExplanationCorrect": "Under ASC 740, net operating loss (NOL) carryforwards create deferred tax assets because they represent future deductible amounts that will reduce taxable income in subsequent periods. A valuation allowance may be required if it is more likely than not that some portion of the DTA will not be realized, but the NOL itself generates a temporary difference, not a permanent difference. Deferred tax liabilities arise from taxable (future income-increasing) temporary differences.",
