    "Stem": "Constrained resource optimization focuses on:",
    "ExplanationCorrect": "When a production constraint (bottleneck) exists, the optimal product mix is determined by maximizing the contribution margin per unit of the constrained resource, not by total volume or total contribution margin alone. The decision rule is: rank products by CM per unit of the binding constraint and produce the highest-ranked products first until the constraint is fully utilized. For example, if Machine Hours are the constraint and Product X has CM of $30 requiring 2 MH (CM/hr = $15) while Product Y has CM of $40 requiring 4 MH (CM/hr = $10), Product X should be prioritized despite having a lower total CM. This is tested under CMA Part 1 Section D.5 (Cost Management — relevant costing and decision analysis). A common exam trap is ranking products by total contribution margin per unit rather than by contribution margin per unit of the scarce resource.",
