    "Stem": "A company's IT audit team is evaluating controls over the information systems environment. They review data center physical security, logical access controls, program change management procedures, and backup and recovery processes. Under the COSO framework, these controls are best categorized as:",
    "CorrectChoice": "A",
    "ExplanationCorrect": "IT general controls (ITGCs) are controls that apply to all or many IT systems and support the effective functioning of application controls. They create the environment in which application controls operate. Common categories of IT general controls include: (1) data center and physical security — controls over physical access to IT facilities and hardware; (2) logical access controls — controls over electronic access to systems, programs, and data, including authentication, authorization, and user provisioning; (3) program change management — controls over the development, testing, and implementation of system changes to ensure only authorized and tested changes are moved to production; and (4) backup and recovery — controls to ensure data can be restored and operations resumed after a disruption. All four areas under review fit squarely within the IT general controls domain because they apply broadly across the IT environment rather than to specific business process transactions. Application controls, by contrast, are embedded within specific software applications and address the completeness, accuracy, validity, and authorization of individual transactions.",
