    "ExplanationCorrect": "The 2013 COSO Framework expanded the five components from the 1992 Framework by articulating 17 principles that represent fundamental concepts associated with each component: (1) Control Environment (5 principles) — includes demonstrating commitment to integrity and ethical values, exercising board oversight responsibility, establishing structure/authority/responsibility, demonstrating commitment to competence, and enforcing accountability; (2) Risk Assessment (4 principles) — includes specifying suitable objectives, identifying and analyzing risks, assessing fraud risk, and identifying and analyzing significant change; (3) Control Activities (3 principles) — includes selecting and developing control activities, selecting and developing general controls over technology, and deploying through policies and procedures; (4) Information and Communication (3 principles) — includes using relevant information, communicating internally, and communicating externally; and (5) Monitoring Activities (2 principles) — includes conducting ongoing and/or separate evaluations, and evaluating and communicating deficiencies. The pair 'Monitoring Activities — Evaluating and communicating control deficiencies' is correct because Principle 17 (the final principle) requires management to evaluate identified control deficiencies and communicate them to parties responsible for corrective action, including senior management and the board as appropriate.",
